From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: a freed view's range goes in sorted order when its neighbours share a granule

free_ranges_remove_view finds the range at the view's granule-rounded base, then moves the base past a granule the
previous view shares. With a view at 0x594000 after one ending there (an emulator splits placeholders on 16 KiB pages),
the range it had found ended at 0x590000, before the moved base, and the new range [0x5a0000, 0x64940000) was put in
front of [0, 0x590000). The list stopped being sorted; the binary search later returned a live guest view's address
to a thread stack and create_view asserted (view->protect & VPROT_SYSTEM): a Unity game's AssetGarbageCollector
thread was not created (2026-10-14, record removed from the tree; in git history). Find the range again from the moved base.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -1486,6 +1486,14 @@
         view_base = prev_view_end;
     if (next_view_base && next_view_base < view_end && next_view_end > view_base)
         view_end = next_view_base;
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* The neighbours can move view_base past a granule the previous view shares (a view at 0x594000 after one
+     * ending there: an emulator's placeholders are split on 16 KiB pages). The range found for the old view_base then
+     * ends before it, and the new free range went in front of it: the list stopped being sorted, the search later
+     * gave a thread stack the address of a live view and create_view asserted (2026-10-14). */
+    range = free_ranges_lower_bound( view_base );
+    next = range + 1;
+#endif
 
     TRACE_(virtual_ranges)( "%p - %p, aligned %p - %p.\n",
                             view->base, (char *)view->base + view->size, view_base, view_end );
